1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:04,780
Your phone can find you to within
about five metres, out under open sky.

2
00:00:04,780 --> 00:00:07,510
It does it by listening
to clocks in space.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:11,540
More than thirty GPS
satellites circle the Earth,

4
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:14,000
about twenty thousand kilometres up.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,630
Each carries atomic clocks, and broadcasts
the exact time and its own position,

6
00:00:18,630 --> 00:00:19,630
over and over.

7
00:00:20,930 --> 00:00:23,600
Your phone notes when each signal arrives.

8
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:28,320
The signal travels at the speed of light,
so the delay reveals the distance.

9
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,810
From a satellite overhead,

10
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:33,480
about seven hundredths of a second
means twenty thousand kilometres.

11
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:38,400
One distance puts you somewhere on a
giant sphere around that satellite.

12
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,680
A second distance narrows it down.

13
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:42,780
A third leaves a single point.

14
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,930
And a fourth satellite corrects
the cheap clock inside your phone.

15
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:49,360
That's why timing is everything.

16
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:52,330
A clock that is off by just one
millionth of a second puts you

17
00:00:52,330 --> 00:00:54,500
about three hundred
metres from where you are.

18
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,380
And the satellite clocks do
drift, because of Einstein.

19
00:00:59,380 --> 00:01:03,020
Their speed slows them by
about seven microseconds a day.

20
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:06,620
The weaker gravity up there
speeds them up by forty five.

21
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:10,220
Overall, they gain thirty eight
microseconds every day.

22
00:01:11,310 --> 00:01:15,690
Left alone, that would add roughly
ten kilometres of error every day.

23
00:01:15,690 --> 00:01:19,940
So before launch, engineers set the
satellite clocks to tick slightly slow.

24
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:23,930
GPS is really a timing system.

25
00:01:23,930 --> 00:01:27,090
Get the time right,
and your position follows.
